course: dictionary
lesson: 4963
title: A word for events
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: An incident is something that happens, especially something unusual, unpleasant or dangerous. Look at the words around it for clues. «The school trip went by without incident.» Without incident means nothing bad or unusual happened on the trip.
explain: Teachers write incident reports when something happens at school, such as a fall or a fight. «Serious incidents like suspensions are written on a pupil's school record.» The clue is the record: an incident here is an event serious enough to be written down.
explain: In news and police reports, incident is a formal word for a crime, accident or fight. «No more of those regrettable incidents with the police» means events someone is sorry about. Always ask: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence.
fact: An incident is something that happens, especially something unusual, unpleasant or dangerous.
fact: «Without incident» means nothing bad or unusual happened.
fact: «A minor incident» means a small event that does not matter much.
fact: In police and news reports, incident is a formal word for a crime, accident or fight.
fact: «Serious incidents» can be written on a pupil's school record, which a new school can see.
exercise: «The school trip went by without incident.» What does without incident mean? | *Nothing unusual or bad happened | The trip was cancelled | Everyone got lost | The bus broke down twice
exercise: A teacher writes an incident report after a fall in the playground. What is the incident here? | A type of school dinner | *An event that happened, such as a fall | A new game for lunchtime | A school holiday
exercise: «The fire drill was only a minor incident.» What does a minor incident suggest? | A kind of sports match | A huge disaster | *A small event that does not matter much | A famous person's visit
test: The class got home «without incident». What does this mean? | They got home late | Everyone was very tired | They lost their bags | *Nothing bad or unusual happened
test: Which sentence uses incident for an event worth reporting? | The class sang a song | The pupil had a quiet, happy lunch | The sky was blue all day | *The pupil was hurt in a playground incident, so a teacher wrote a report
exam: «Serious incidents are written on a pupil's school record.» Why would a school write an incident down? | Because it was a happy day | Because the school wants a new lunch | To make the pupil famous | *Because it was an event serious enough to record
